  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + gate">Load task, project CLAUDE.md, HANDOFF doc, the eval README + suite, and the five row mirrors. CONFIRM tasks 040–044 rows exist and core Phase A0 published the eval-gate + dispatch seam before authoring.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Author golden families">For each of the five rows, add ≥5 golden-utterance cases (phrasings, typos, doc-level triggers as appropriate) asserting correct dispatch, consumerType/consumerCode, and schemaConformance against the row's OutputSchemaJson.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Author dispatch families">For each row, add ≥5 dispatch cases exercising the Click-path seam (and, for compose-draft-alternative, the `compose`-disposition ledger write; for compose-summarize-word-changes, the return-from-Word invocation).</step>
    <step order="3" name="Schema validation">Run the OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator catalog contract test + jps-validate over all five schemas; confirm no property-level boolean `required`.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Green CI">Run the eval suite; confirm all families green and inventory integrity passes.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Eval/golden-utterances.json (golden + dispatch families for 5 rows)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Eval/GoldenUtteranceEvalSuiteTests.cs (coverage extension if needed)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Each of the five rows has a golden-utterance family AND a dispatch family, ≥5 cases each (10 families total, ≥50 cases).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every case asserts closed-catalog dispatch through the shipped seam and schemaConformance against the row's OutputSchemaJson; no case references a second intent-detection mechanism or tool-name gating list.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All five Action OutputSchemaJson pass OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator with NO property-level boolean `required` (contract test green).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The compose-draft-alternative dispatch family asserts the `compose`-disposition ledger write; the compose-summarize-word-changes family asserts return-from-Word invocation.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The eval suite is green in CI; no banned test shape is introduced; no row lacking coverage is merge-eligible.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Consumes core Phase A0 eval-gate + triple-twin description hoist + session-dispatch/invoke seam per notes/HANDOFF-core-r2-A0-contract-requirements.md §7. If the published contract differs from the proposed shape, STOP and reconcile — do not adapt silently.</trigger>
  </escalation>

